### JWT Authentication - Product API
### This file contains HTTP request examples to test JWT authentication

### 1. Login - Get JWT Token
POST https://localhost:7000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Validate Token (copy the token from the response above)
GET https://localhost:7000/api/auth/validate
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 3. Access Product WITH authentication (replace the token)
GET https://localhost:7000/api/products/123
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 4. Access Product WITHOUT authentication (should return 401)
GET https://localhost:7000/api/products/123

###
### NOTES:
### - Default password for any user is: password123
### - Token expires in 60 minutes (configurable in appsettings.json)
### - To test in Swagger, click the "Authorize" button and paste the token
###

